That's one of the roadblocks in Nethack that you have to learn to deal
with. They are (in mostly chronological order) floating eyes, nymphs,
leprecauns, rothes (along with the other q's you run across later),
soldier ants, mordor orcs (only for poison reasons), Rust monsters,
Polymorph traps, Level teleport traps, Vampires, mindflayers, Liches and
then on to the named Monsters. There's a couple left out like bugbears,
and the Dragons but the point is that half of the game is *knowing* how
to deal with each of them when they appear and the other half is knowing
what sort of AC and weapon skill you need for level x or sidebranch y.
You only get to know that by playing repeatedly. The other thing is to
build up your basic tool kit as early as possible. These are an uncursed
sack of some kind, a key/lockpick/credit card, a blindfold/towel and a
pick of some kind for digging. After that you really only need to get
good at a weapon, a projectile weapon and steadily better AC. That alone
will take you down to the 15-20th level. 

